From: patrickjquinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wmt: log expected states at debug level

wmt_plat_wake_lock_ctrl() warned on every nested wake lock get and put
("wakelock status(n), counter(m)"), which is the normal case whenever
more than one CONNSYS function holds the lock; only the first get and
the last put change anything, and those already log at debug.

wmt_ctrl_get_rom_patch_info() logged "NULL patchinfo pointer" as an
error for each patch type the firmware has no ROM patch for, although
it returns 1 for that case and mtk_wcn_soc_rom_patch_dwn() treats 1 as
"nothing to download" and logs it itself. A SOC2_2 CONNSYS has ROM
patches for BT, Wi-Fi and the MCU only, so FM and GNSS logged an error
on every power-up.

Log both at debug level.
---
--- a/wmt_drv/common_main/core/wmt_ctrl.c
+++ b/wmt_drv/common_main/core/wmt_ctrl.c
@@ -696,7 +696,7 @@
 			WMT_DBG_FUNC("get 4 address bytes is 0x%2x,0x%2x,0x%2x,0x%2x",
 					pAbuf[0], pAbuf[1], pAbuf[2], pAbuf[3]);
 		} else {
-			WMT_ERR_FUNC("NULL patchinfo pointer\n");
+			WMT_DBG_FUNC("no rom patch of type %u\n", type);
 			ret = 1;
 		}
 	} else {
--- a/wmt_drv/common_main/platform/wmt_plat_alps.c
+++ b/wmt_drv/common_main/platform/wmt_plat_alps.c
@@ -1623,7 +1623,7 @@
 		WMT_DBG_FUNC("WMT-PLAT: after wake_unlock(%d), counter(%d)\n",
 				osal_wake_lock_count(&wmt_wake_lock), counter);
 	} else {
-		WMT_WARN_FUNC("WMT-PLAT: wakelock status(%d), counter(%d)\n",
+		WMT_DBG_FUNC("WMT-PLAT: wakelock status(%d), counter(%d)\n",
 				osal_wake_lock_count(&wmt_wake_lock), counter);
 	}
 
